#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068432 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3674f343-59bc-5420-9dca-44102b11aba6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "a474788c-5b2b-570d-84bf-2c9575ac4f54" :question/math-academy-id "e-10022" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{8z^3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $8z^3$ as the product $4z^2 \\cdot 2z$ which contains a perfect square $(4z^2){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{8z^3}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2\\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2|\\cdot|z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n\t2|z|\\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4df00200-f680-53f3-9b49-700b9ac14204" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square With Domain Restrictions"}] :question/id #uuid "969be012-a830-564e-a355-00a4f1985ae8" :question/math-academy-id "e-1363" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{18y^3}$ given that $y \\geq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $18y^3$ as the product $9y^2\\cdot 2y$ which contains a perfect square $(9y^2).$ Then, we separate the product into two separate radicals, one of which can be simplified:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sqrt{18y^3} &= \\\n\t\t\\sqrt{9y^2 \\cdot 2y} &= \\\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\\sqrt{9y^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t\\sqrt{(3y)^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t|3y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\t\t\n\t\t|3| \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3 \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y}\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince $y \\geq 0,$ we have $|y|=y,$ and we can simplify further. Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3 \\cdot |y| \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3 \\cdot y \\cdot \\sqrt{2y} &= \\\n\t\t3y\\sqrt{2y}. &\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068676 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2471751-7e5c-5823-9f63-76d14f927db2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square With Larger Powers"}] :question/id #uuid "ce2e3248-96e3-5d69-9a16-1a62e0ce0eeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-9980" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{50u^7}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $50u^7$ as the product $25u^6\\cdot 2u$ which contains a perfect square $(25u^6){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{50u^7}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5|\\cdot |u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t5|u|^3 \\sqrt{2u}\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3674f343-59bc-5420-9dca-44102b11aba6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a85dfae-b58e-5110-b0b2-b9912f1cccfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500584} {:answer/id #uuid "5b029b06-3fe8-5023-a99f-576ac04f043d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9y\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500654} {:answer/id #uuid "ae31e598-f5ee-5a89-8202-3e24a0c7c88b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500828} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a4c910-97b2-5aac-ba3f-9b72d7d1e641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9|y|\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500958} {:answer/id #uuid "f81c3cae-04ac-5c1d-9a0e-992240cc9e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|y|\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f81c3cae-04ac-5c1d-9a0e-992240cc9e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|y|\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500996} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cd740e-2e2f-5d86-98a0-50d1b58bfb81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b89f2670-8d2c-52b5-b612-dd1804214943" :question/math-academy-id "q-141464" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{54{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $54{y}^{2}$ as the product $9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6$ which contains a perfect square $(9{y}^{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{54{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{9{y}^{2}\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(3y)^{2}\\cdot 6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(3y)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(3y)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ |3y|\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ |3|\\cdot |y|\\cdot \\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 3|y|\\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2471751-7e5c-5823-9f63-76d14f927db2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square With Larger Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5741f9cd-2501-5b30-b7e0-a278215b6fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500643} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a8333c-e258-5e91-8543-659cd1e80ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500843} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb9a3f1-55c2-57c9-b329-b187936a94f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500903} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b43e48-be98-5967-b286-728ee8cbc556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11|u{|}^{8}\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500943} {:answer/id #uuid "f25b5c8a-e6b1-58c5-abb0-68b7842aaaf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|u{|}^{8}\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb9a3f1-55c2-57c9-b329-b187936a94f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500903} :answer-field/id #uuid "532d42ad-6983-5ac0-b812-0adeaa85ae60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2d5742a-0261-5618-8222-f4f0f769fb79" :question/math-academy-id "q-141477" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{44{u}^{8}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $44{u}^{8}$ as the product $4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11$ which contains a perfect square $(4{u}^{8}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{44{u}^{8}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{u}^{8}\\cdot 11} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}\\cdot 11} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(2{u}^{4})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ |2{u}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ |2|\\cdot |{u}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{11} & = \\\\ 2|u{|}^{4}\\sqrt{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3674f343-59bc-5420-9dca-44102b11aba6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression That Is Not a Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2151c7cd-e6ab-52e8-9366-584c9ea7f941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{r}^{2}\\sqrt{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500536} {:answer/id #uuid "321221f6-baac-50eb-978c-4a7948aff069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5|r|\\sqrt{5r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500572} {:answer/id #uuid "644eff91-0f4b-5176-bf9d-5c3031d27583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{r}^{2}\\sqrt{5r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500677} {:answer/id #uuid "7813cfa6-4b6c-57be-975c-44d185242f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|r|\\sqrt{5r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500717} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca20a89-e601-5fc3-8b5a-f7ecb7cc0938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5|r|\\sqrt{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ca20a89-e6